// Core device-extent access authority.
//
// A DMA transfer is an external borrow of an `Extent` range by a device the
// checker cannot see. `DeviceLoan` is the linear proxy for that borrow: public
// opaque data whose runtime identity is owned by the selected provider. Source
// can carry it between boundary crossings but can never construct, copy, or
// inspect it — direction, confinement, provenance, and completion obligations
// are provider admission evidence, not source representation, and no package
// can reconstruct a loan from fields.
//
// `DeviceReads` carries the shared borrow: the device observes the range while
// ordinary CPU mutation is excluded. `DeviceWrites` carries the exclusive
// borrow: all CPU access is excluded until completion. Direction is part of
// the borrow's canonical identity and is established only by the admitted
// lend crossing; reconstruction, forgery, or a reproduced loan copy
// establishes neither.
//
// Ordering roles are provider-issued opaque occurrences: a `DeviceOrderingEvent`
// is the linear record of one protocol step — publication, cache maintenance,
// notification, or completion — bound to the exact loan, range, mapping,
// device instance, and runtime scope at admission. Equal payloads under
// different roles are not interchangeable: the role is part of the event's
// canonical identity and only the admitted establishing crossing mints it.
// Source carries and retires occurrences but can never mint, compare, or
// inspect them. `settle` consumes any carried occurrence the protocol retires;
// `notify` consumes a valid publication and requalifies it notification —
// an intersecting write between publication and notification invalidates the
// carried record at the provider, which the notify crossing then rejects.
//
// `complete` is the provider's completion obligation: it consumes a live loan
// of either direction and either yields the `Completion` occurrence — borrower
// release proven, custody still suspended — or returns the still-live
// `Pending` loan for retry. `acquire` consumes that completion occurrence and
// either restores the range's Stable CPU custody as `Extent::Granted` or
// returns the retained completion candidate for retry. Custody is restored
// only after borrower release and every ordering/coherence obligation; a CPU
// barrier or device status alone establishes neither. An ordinary call can
// mint none of these facts.
//
// Device protocols, DMA queue submission, and IPC ownership remain
// consumer/provider code; this module publishes only the general authority
// vocabulary (wiki/spec/resources/device_access.md).
use omega::language::core::extent;

public boundary data DeviceLoan [linear];

public domain DeviceLoan::DeviceReads
established by
    DeviceLoanProvider::lend_for_read;
public domain DeviceLoan::DeviceWrites
established by
    DeviceLoanProvider::lend_for_write;

// The linear proxy for one provider-issued ordering occurrence. Its runtime
// identity is owned by the selected provider exactly like the loan proxy:
// opaque to source, unforgeable by construction, and meaningful only through
// the admitted role crossings below.
public boundary data DeviceOrderingEvent [linear];

public domain DeviceOrderingEvent::Publication
established by
    DeviceLoanProvider::publish;
public domain DeviceOrderingEvent::CacheMaintenance
established by
    DeviceLoanProvider::maintain_cache;
public domain DeviceOrderingEvent::Notification
established by
    DeviceLoanProvider::notify;

// The proven completion occurrence rides inside the `DeviceCompletionAttempt`
// carrier rather than being returned directly, so the domain — like the
// shootdown debt's `Owed` — has no `established by` crossing of its own.
public domain DeviceOrderingEvent::Completion;

// Completion custody: the proven `Completion` occurrence on success, or the
// still-live loan when the provider could not prove borrower release — the
// caller retries `complete` with it rather than losing custody.
public data DeviceCompletionAttempt {
    case Completed(completion: DeviceOrderingEvent in DeviceOrderingEvent::Completion);
    case Pending(loan: DeviceLoan);
}

// Acquisition custody: the restored `Granted` range on success, or the
// retained completion candidate for a later `acquire` retry.
public data DeviceAcquisitionAttempt {
    case Acquired(extent: Extent in Granted);
    case Pending(completion: DeviceOrderingEvent in DeviceOrderingEvent::Completion);
}

// The domain owner authorizes exactly these admitted loan crossings. The
// caller supplies a `Granted` range; the selected provider plan's admission
// receipt is what establishes the direction qualification on the returned
// proxy, binding borrower, direction, space, provenance, rights, and the
// completion obligation with an exact confinement receipt.
public boundary trait DeviceLoanProvider {
    // Reserves `length` bytes in the provider's own address-space pool: the
    // ranges a device may borrow are the ranges the same authority
    // provisioned, so the pool owner — not an extent-geometry caller — mints
    // the `Granted` claim. A hosted entry supplies no arrival extents; this
    // is the only `Granted` source a hosted program reaches today.
    machine reserve(length: u64) -> Extent
    reaches
    ensures
        result in Extent::Granted;

    // Returns a restored range's `Granted` authority to the provider's pool,
    // ending the caller's claim. Every reserved extent terminates here or
    // beneath a frame that never exits.
    machine release(range: Extent in Granted) reaches;

    machine lend_for_read(range: Extent in Granted) -> DeviceLoan
    reaches
    ensures
        result in DeviceLoan::DeviceReads;

    machine lend_for_write(range: Extent in Granted) -> DeviceLoan
    reaches
    ensures
        result in DeviceLoan::DeviceWrites;

    // Publication names the live loan's range and current write state. An
    // intersecting CPU write after this crossing invalidates the occurrence
    // before `notify` may consume it.
    machine publish(loan: &DeviceLoan) -> DeviceOrderingEvent
    reaches
    ensures
        result in DeviceOrderingEvent::Publication;

    // Provider cache maintenance over the live loan's range: the target's
    // fence/cache facts admitted for this loan's space and direction, bound
    // as an occurrence the caller retires through `settle`. An
    // instruction-free coherent realization produces no occurrence here —
    // it simply has nothing to report.
    machine maintain_cache(loan: &DeviceLoan) -> DeviceOrderingEvent
    reaches
    ensures
        result in DeviceOrderingEvent::CacheMaintenance;

    // Notification consumes a still-valid publication: the provider delivers
    // the recorded notification and requalifies the occurrence, or rejects a
    // publication an intersecting write already invalidated.
    machine notify(publication: DeviceOrderingEvent in DeviceOrderingEvent::Publication) -> DeviceOrderingEvent
    reaches
    ensures
        result in DeviceOrderingEvent::Notification;

    // Retire one carried occurrence the protocol no longer needs. `settle`
    // consumes the event; it restores no custody and establishes no
    // completion, access, or ordering fact.
    machine settle(event: DeviceOrderingEvent) reaches;

    // The completion obligation: consumes the live loan. On proven borrower
    // release the `Completed` case carries the `Completion` occurrence for
    // `acquire`; otherwise the `Pending` case returns the still-live loan so
    // the caller may retry — a failed start of the release never strands the
    // borrow.
    machine complete(loan: DeviceLoan) -> DeviceCompletionAttempt reaches;

    // Acquisition consumes a `Completion` occurrence tied to the same request,
    // loan, device, and scope: `Acquired` restores the range's Stable CPU
    // custody, `Pending` returns the retained completion candidate for retry.
    machine acquire(completion: DeviceOrderingEvent in DeviceOrderingEvent::Completion) -> DeviceAcquisitionAttempt reaches;
}
